# Supabase project (client-safe values only — the anon key is public by design;
# security comes from RLS). Leave unset to run the app on the built-in
# localStorage dev backend (no Supabase required).
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# --- Edge Function secrets (set via `supabase secrets set`, NEVER exposed to
# --- the client; listed here for documentation only) ---
# FIGMA_CLIENT_ID=
# FIGMA_CLIENT_SECRET=
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=  (provided automatically inside Edge Functions)
#
# Submission notifications (v2). The sender lives on the agency's own domain:
# complete SendGrid domain authentication for it before launch (SendGrid
# generates the SPF/DKIM CNAME records; the agency adds them at its own
# registrar) or mail lands in spam. An unverified sender fails with a 403 at
# send time, not at deploy time.
# SENDGRID_API_KEY=
# NOTIFICATION_FROM_EMAIL=    e.g. admin@themercenarynetwork.com
# NOTIFICATION_FROM_NAME=     optional display name, e.g. Signature Content
# PUBLIC_APP_URL=             deployed origin, for review deep links in email
